<title>BELGIUM: FINOUTREMER, AGRICOM PROFIT UP.</title>
<headline>FINOUTREMER, AGRICOM PROFIT UP.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to 30 June, 1996</p>
<p>(in thousands of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>Group net (excludes minorities)	   193.58  vs  175.09</p>
<p>Consolidated net				201.74  vs  180.12</p>
<p>Consolidated current			  232.16  vs  210.96</p>
<p>Exceptional loss				 25.34  vs  18.93</p>
<p>Taxation					    5.26  vs  12.23</p>
<p>Group earnings/share (in francs)	     151  vs  137</p>
<p>NOTE - Cie Financiere Europeenne et d'Outre-Mer SA said that while 1996 H1 current profit was slightly higher, it continued to be influenced by weakness in African activities.</p>
<p>Finoutremer said it expected to pay a 1996 dividend at least equal to that paid in 1995. It said net asset value per share had risen to 5,621 francs at 30 September 1996.</p>
<p>Results for the six months to 30 June for Finoutremer subsidiary Agricom SA (in millions of Belgian francs)</p>
<p>Net profit					57.8  vs  55.6</p>
<p>Current					   61.5  vs  59.6</p>
<p>Exceptional loss				 0.4  vs  n/a</p>
<p>Estimated taxation			     3.3  vs   4</p>
<p>Net per share (in francs)		   21.9  vs  21</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +322 287 6810, Fax +322 230 7710</p>
</text>
